<Placemark>
	<name>Awaru Old Airstrip</name>
	<description><![CDATA[<!-- desc_gen:start -->
<font color="black"><table width="100%"><tr><td width="100%" align="center"><a href="files/1000017075.jpg" target="_blank"><img src="files/1000017075.jpg" width="60px" align="right" style="border: 3px white solid;"></a><br /><br /><a href="files/1000058227.jpg" target="_blank"><img src="files/1000058227.jpg" width="60px" align="right" style="border: 3px white solid;"></a><br /><br />
<!-- desc_user:start -->
The soccer field at Awaru was cleared in the early 2000s as an airstrip. It was cleared after flights to Sila stopped due to a clan dispute between two brothers over the airstrip there. Once the dispute was resolved and flights resumed at Sila, the Awaru airstrip was abandoned and later houses were built on part of the land and the remaining area became a soccer field.
<!-- desc_user:end -->
</td></tr><tr><td colspan="1"><hr></td></tr><tr><td><table width="100%"><tr><td align="left" valign="center"><small><b>Altitude</b></small></td><td align="center" valign="center">688 m</td></tr>
